  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI set up my second homeserver, however when trying to invite users from other homeservers, server signature verification fails with a message similar to `M_UNAUTHORIZED: Invalid signature for server matrix.org with key ed25519:a_RXGa: Unable to verify signature for matrix.org: <class 'nacl.exceptions.BadSignatureError'> Signature was forged or corrupt`. I couldn't figure out a way to make it work, I even tried recreating the signing key and pruning the server database. Everything works if I make it silently ignore verification errors. Everything works on my first homeserver as well, which uses the same nginx and postgres config. The major difference is new server is using arm and the old one is using x86.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- create a homeserver\r\n- ???\r\n- profit\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Version**: 1.40.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: pip\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: linux, arm64, oracle linux 8 on oracle cloud with latest updates\r\n",
